cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the original
  paper it reproduces (listed under references).
type: software
title: "Hiv-Drc-Model: a tested reproduction of the DRC HIV/AIDS treatment model, with parameter estimation from noisy data"
authors:
  - alias: heinricitorgau
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24274982
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24274982
    description: Zenodo concept DOI (all versions; resolves to the latest)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24274983
    description: Zenodo DOI of version 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/heinricitorgau/hiv-drc-model"
abstract: >-
  A reproduction of the six-compartment HIV/AIDS transmission model with
  treatment of Mbayi, Mpompi and Munyakazi (Tamkang Journal of Mathematics,
  2026), extended with the inverse problem: recovering transmission and
  treatment rates from noisy surveillance data by bounded nonlinear least
  squares and ensemble MCMC, observation operators for UNAIDS indicators,
  time-varying rates, and an evaluation against real DRC data.
keywords:
  - epidemiology
  - compartmental model
  - HIV
  - basic reproduction number
  - inverse problem
  - parameter estimation
  - bayesian inference
  - MCMC
  - uncertainty quantification
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A model of HIV/AIDS transmission dynamics with treatment: The case of the DRC"
    authors:
      - family-names: Mbayi
        given-names: Charles K.
      - family-names: Mpompi
        given-names: Jean-Marie N.
      - family-names: Munyakazi
        given-names: Justin B.
    journal: Tamkang Journal of Mathematics
    volume: 57
    issue: 2
    start: 149
    end: 169
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.5556/j.tkjm.57.5817.2026
